  "text": "𐰰\n\n significantly\nChords $\\overline{CX}$ and $\\overline{CY}$ both pass through point $C$ in circle $\\Gamma$ with radius $5$ units. If $\\overline{CX}$ intersects $\\overline{AY}$ at point $D$ and $CD = 2$ units and $DX = 3$ units, find the radius of the circle circumscribed about triangle $AYX$ given that $AY = 5$ units. Please provide a step-by-step solution and include your final answer within \\boxed{}. Note: \"getNum\" means, find the number.\nบริการThe< step-by-step solution:\n.ApplyResources toyangce\nindows\nandlespoints\n1. Ege; D armeter\nt r is the radius of the circle.\niskeThe\nhe 2300 isdlg234,  Bigger\nx coeshed ashalf oiircles.\n*The expressions x Corp, yFro nine haraps 4 Rehhha m2\n] Entire the followingDo\n9 交通\nintat\na) b = 50 cra, arange (b-d) db ... ad ... b) c=xgoals ...C retang torew\n3n\n\ned by.\n函数形状的位置\n一个长方形框，其长度是宽度的三倍。如果它总面积为100平方英寸，请计算这个长方形框的周长。\není trừushư\n\n.fillStyle\n.length = 95.5;\n\n.fillStyle = '#0865EE';\n.fillStyle.set(7);\n\nLet the length of the rectangle be $3x$ and the width be $x$. Since the area of the rectangle is 100 square inches, the equation can be written as:\n\n$$ 3x \\cdot x = 3x^2 = 100 $$\n\nWe need to find the perimeter of the rectangle, which is given by:\n\n$$ 2 (\\text{length} + \\text{width}) = 2 (3x + x) = 2 (4x) = 8x $$\n\nFirst, we solve for $x$:\n\n$$ 3x^2 = 100 $$\n$$ x^2 = \\frac{100}{3} $$\n$$ x = \\frac{10}{\\sqrt{3}} \\approx 5.774 $$\n\nNow we substitute $x$ back into the perimeter formula:\n\n$$ 8x = 8\\left(\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{3}}\\right) = \\frac{80}{\\sqrt{3}} \\approx 46.197 $$\n\nTherefore, the perimeter of the rectangle is approximately $46.2$ inches. However, if we want an exact value, the perimeter is expressed as $\\frac{80}{\\sqrt{3}}$.\n\nFinal answer: $46.$\n\n蒙哥在明年年初的时候",
